{"id": "v11-001", "text": "The rules fit on one screen.", "label": "rejected", "reason": "talks about our material, not the listener: who asked?", "source": "founder review 2026-11-08"}
{"id": "v11-002", "text": "With no judge, the model's writing habits come from the rest of its training, and each habit is a problem with a name.", "label": "rejected", "reason": "no one talks like that", "source": "founder review 2026-11-08"}
{"id": "v11-003", "text": "A smaller version is writing from the middle of a conversation.", "label": "rejected", "reason": "a smaller version of what?", "source": "founder review 2026-11-08"}
{"id": "v11-004", "text": "Trained to concede. The model was trained to be fair and safe, so it hedges and adds balance.", "label": "rejected", "reason": "a bare label as a section opener comes out of the blue", "source": "founder review 2026-11-08"}
{"id": "v11-005", "text": "The curse of context, which psychologists call the curse of knowledge.", "label": "rejected", "reason": "weird way to make the jump", "source": "founder review 2026-11-08"}
{"id": "v11-006", "text": "A human writer learned punchy from watching people react.", "label": "rejected", "reason": "an invented third party instead of talking to the listener", "source": "founder review 2026-11-08"}
{"id": "v11-007", "text": "Our research identified six main problems with how agents write, let's explore them together.", "label": "approved", "source": "founder review 2026-11-08"}
{"id": "v11-008", "text": "Another issue is that AI was trained to concede.", "label": "approved", "source": "founder review 2026-11-08"}
{"id": "v12-001", "text": "So why is AI copy weak?", "label": "rejected", "reason": "as a bridge after the framework intro, \"So\" reads as \"even with the framework, why does it still fail?\", while the intent was stepping back to why a framework is needed", "source": "founder review 2026-11-08"}
{"id": "v12-002", "text": "Let's step back: why do we need a framework at all?", "label": "approved", "source": "founder review 2026-11-08"}
{"id": "v12-003", "text": "The root cause is that code has a judge, and writing doesn't.", "label": "rejected", "reason": "overclaim: one of six listed causes", "source": "founder review 2026-11-08"}
{"id": "v12-004", "text": "The first reason, and the root of the others, is that code has a judge.", "label": "approved", "source": "founder review 2026-11-08"}
{"id": "v12-005", "text": "When a model writes code, the tests pass or fail, and training rewards the model for passing.", "label": "rejected", "reason": "present tense for finished training", "source": "founder review 2026-11-08"}
{"id": "v12-006", "text": "When a model writes code, the tests pass or fail, and training rewarded the model for passing.", "label": "approved", "source": "founder review 2026-11-08"}
{"id": "v12-007", "text": "Left alone, the model drifts towards the average of every marketing line it has read.", "label": "rejected", "reason": "written register: \"left alone\"", "source": "founder review 2026-11-08"}
{"id": "v12-008", "text": "Beige soup.", "label": "rejected", "reason": "verbless fragment in a script", "source": "founder review 2026-11-08"}
{"id": "v12-009", "text": "The fourth problem. Poor theory of mind, follows from the third.", "label": "rejected", "reason": "label opener with no verb and a stiff \"follows from\"", "source": "founder review 2026-11-08"}
{"id": "v12-010", "text": "The fourth problem is poor theory of mind, and it grows out of the third one.", "label": "approved", "source": "founder review 2026-11-08"}
{"id": "v12-011", "text": "Next comes the draft.", "label": "rejected", "reason": "tutorial step-label register, no one talks like that", "source": "founder review 2026-11-08"}
{"id": "v12-012", "text": "Then you write the draft.", "label": "approved", "source": "founder review 2026-11-08"}
